    "result_text": "No stray references. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`. Verified via the audit log (`memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`) and **BUILD SUCCESS / Tests run: 1, Failures: 0**.\n\n**What changed (5 files):**\n\n1. **`MemberId.java`** (new) \u2014 one small, cohesive helper: `of(region, registrationDate, hash8)` builds the id (fiscal year + HASH8 + Luhn `CHK` over the preceding digits via the existing `CheckDigit`), and `region(...)` / `fiscalYear(...)` parse the fixed-width tail so derived fields can reference the id.\n2. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 one line: stores the full `memberId` instead of `REGION-HASH8`.\n3. **`SaveOwner.java`** \u2014 the audit record now logs `memberId` (dropped the `membershipNumber`/`customerCode` fields).\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `memberId`; removed `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit`; repointed `fiscalYear`, `ownerSegment`, `locality`, and `timezone` at `MemberId` (fiscal year and owner segment now reference the id, per spec).\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`/`checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` schema properties with a single `memberId`.\n\n**Keeping structural impact low:**\n- The dedup step (`DeduplicateCustomerCode`) needed **no change** \u2014 it already dedupes the stored code generically, so collision handling now applies to the `memberId` for free.\n- Left the internal entity field/column named `customer_code` (it now holds the memberId), avoiding edits to `Owner.java`, its getters/setters, and every caller \u2014 the entity name is internal and not part of the spec's field-removal requirement.\n- New behavior lives in `MemberId`'s three tiny methods (CC 1 each, near-zero surrounding complexity) rather than growing `AssignCustomerCode`, the mapper expressions, or the entity.\n\n`MembershipNumber.java` and `CheckDigit.java` remain; `CheckDigit` is still used (by `MemberId`), and `MembershipNumber` is now unused but harmless \u2014 deleting it would touch an extra file for no functional gain.",
